WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
Welcome to this special deep dive edition of Modern Investing Techniques.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:07.660
Today we explore the SpaceX initial public offering process

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.680
in what it means for retail investors.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:14.060
I'm not a licensed financial advisor and this isn't financial advice.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:18.180
Nothing here is a recommendation to buy or sell any security.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.900
Always do your own research before putting real money to work.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:28.320
SpaceX filed its S1 on May 20th targeting a June 12th NASDAQ listing

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.180
at roughly $1.8 trillion valuation.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:36.740
This episode gives retail investors a concrete plan across three time horizons.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:42.100
On May 20th, 2026, SpaceX Exploration Technologies Corporation

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.160
filed its public S1 registration statement with the SEC.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.020
That filing converted months of draft stage speculation into a concrete timeline.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:57.960
The timeline points to pricing around June 11th and first trading as early as June 12th

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.080
under the ticker SPCX. By the end of this episode,

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.260
listeners will know exactly what the filing confirms about valuation targets,

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:09.540
underwriters, and Starlink's contribution to revenue.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.700
They will also leave with a practical three horizon framework for deciding

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.820
whether and how to participate once the stock begins trading.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:22.680
SpaceX filed a confidential draft registration around April 1st, 2026.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.460
The company then converted it to a public S1 on May 20th

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:33.300
under registration number 3333. That step made the prospect as available on Edgar.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:39.520
Reporting from Reuters and CNBC indicates the company is aiming for a listing on NASDAQ

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:45.040
as early as June 12th. The road show is expected to begin around June 4th

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.480
and pricing is targeted for June 11th.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:53.300
The valuation range discussed in recent coverage has settled around $1.75

00:01:53.300 --> 00:02:01.880
2 trillion. Bloomberg noted on May 29th that the target had been adjusted to at least $1.8 trillion.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:06.460
The deal is structured to include Starlink connectivity operations,

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:13.260
launch and space services and XAI. Goldman Sachs is serving as lead left book runner alongside

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:17.280
Morgan Stanley, Bank of America, City Group and JP Morgan.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:22.820
Starlink generated $11.4 billion in revenue in 2025.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:28.720
That amount represented 61% of the company's $18.7 billion total.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.780
Starlink is also the only segment showing operating profit.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.760
The overall business posted a net loss in Q1, 2026.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:43.080
A potential retail allocation near 30% of the float has been mentioned in secondary commentary.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:48.340
That allocation remains unconfirmed in primary filings or major reporting.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:54.840
The 2026 IPO calendar features several large technology and AI-related offerings.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:59.840
This creates a market backdrop of elevated investor interest in growth names,

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:03.040
even as interest rate and risk sentiment remain mixed.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:10.460
The S1 shows that Elon Musk holds approximately 42% of equity, but 85% of voting power.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.420
That structure preserves control through a dual-class arrangement.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.280
The arrangement will matter for governance questions after listing.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:21.980
Starlink is positioned as the cash-generative core.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:27.520
It has more than 10 million subscribers and continued growth into Q1, 2026.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:32.160
Launch operations and XAI continue to consume capital.

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:37.280
Underwriters typically allocate the majority of shares to institutional clients in the initial

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:43.060
offering. Most retail investors will therefore obtain shares only after trading begins,

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:46.340
unless their broker offers a directed share program.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:50.740
Reading the prospectus requires focus on revenue concentration.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:55.740
It also requires attention to the path from operating income to free cash flow.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:01.380
Investors should examine the use of proceeds and any government contract exposure that could

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:09.520
affect margins. Canadian investors must weigh TFSA, RRSP, or FHSA eligibility,

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:13.200
against the fact that the shares will trade in US dollars.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:18.340
That currency exposure can be hedged or left un-hedged, depending on account type.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:23.520
Valuation discipline starts with comparing the targeted multiple to other high-growth

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:29.860
technology names already public. The $1.8 trillion figure implies aggressive assumptions

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:32.360
about subscriber growth and launch economics.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:38.320
Platforms such as interactive brokers, quest trade, wealth simple, and Robinhood will likely

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:45.060
offer post-listing access. Conditional offer to buy windows before pricing remain broker-specific

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:51.160
and are not guaranteed. The filing does not yet detail exact retail allocation mechanics.

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:56.120
Investors should monitor subsequent amendments and broker announcements rather than assume

00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:02.540
early access. A disciplined short-term approach treats the opening days as the highest risk window.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:06.340
First day pops are common but frequently retraced.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:12.420
Wide-bit-ask spreads plus potential volatility around the open make chasing the initial print

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:18.320
expensive for anyone without a preset role. Investors can decide in advance whether they will

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:25.220
participate at all on day one or wait for volume to normalize. That decision removes emotion from

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:32.300
the process. In the medium term, the 180-day lock-up expiry creates a predictable supply event.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:36.060
Early investors and insiders become free to sell at that point.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:41.660
Waiting for that window or dollar-cost averaging afterward has historically reduced entry

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:47.220
prices for comparable names. The first two earnings reports as a public company will supply the

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:52.720
initial evidence on whether Starlink margins and subscriber metrics translate cleanly into gap

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:58.320
results. Over the long term, the thesis rests on recurring satellite broadband revenue.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:03.980
It also rests on Starship-driven launch cost reductions and the broader total addressable

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:09.600
market cited in the filing. Those factors must be balanced against key person risk,

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:14.920
ongoing capital intensity, and competition in both connectivity and launch markets.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:20.660
Canadians should consider whether a taxable account or a registered plan better accommodates the

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:26.640
currency exposure and single stock volatility limits they are willing to accept. Position sizing

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:32.540
should reflect the difference between a diversified ETF holding and a concentrated growth name.

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:39.720
Investors need clear criteria for what subscriber or margin data would confirm or break the investment

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:47.380
case over multiple years. The same horizon framework can be reused for any future large-cap IPO.

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:52.520
Define the entry rule for each period before the stock begins trading.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:56.300
Then execute only according to those pre-written rules.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:02.680
Historical data on large IPOs shows that many names experience first-day gains followed by

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:07.920
underperformance over the subsequent one to three years. That underperformance often occurs

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:12.120
once lock-up supply arrives and fundamentals are tested in public reporting.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:17.460
The current research notes that some analysts view the valuation as aggressive relative

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:23.320
to a sum of parts breakdown. Others highlight the optionality embedded in starship economics

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:29.520
and future businesses. Execution risk remains material because launch cadence, satellite deployment

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:36.260
and regulatory approvals for spectrum and orbital slots must continue at scale. Musk's concentrated

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:42.020
voting control reduces the ability of public shareholders to influence strategy. That control

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:46.920
can be viewed as either a strength or a governance concern depending on execution outcomes.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:52.920
Competition in satellite broadband from established and new entrants could pressure margins even

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:59.380
if starlink grows. The capital demands of both a launch and AI segments had further pressure.

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:05.880
The base rate that IPOs tend to lag broad indices in the first few years after listing is well

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:12.460
documented across multiple market cycles. That base rate should inform any position size decision.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:18.920
Predefine separate entry and sizing rules for the first trading week, the lock-up expiry window

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:23.160
and the multi-year hold period rather than reacting to price action.

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:29.940
Focus first on the quality and concentration of revenue and the path to sustainable free cash flow

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:37.160
in the S1 before considering valuation multiples. Treat any single name growth stock as a satellite

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:42.840
position whose size is caped by personal volatility tolerance and overall portfolio construction

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:48.960
rules. Watch for amendments to the S1 and broker announcements on retail access in the coming weeks.

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:54.960
Then compare those details against the three horizon framework before taking any action.

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:59.340
The show returns to its regular daily markets coverage next episode.

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:06.020
Thanks for listening to modern investing techniques. This episode used AI voice synthesis of my voice.

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:09.080
Editorial selection and analysis are my own.
